# Multi-server vs ENV (current truth)

## Fact (Slice 1 done)

- Per-server SSH: `servers.ssh_*` + encrypted key/password; `await getSshClient(serverId)`.
- Global `SSH_*` = fallback + one-time seed into oldest active server (`ensurePrimaryServerSshFromEnv`).
- Still **global env** (not Slice 1): Coolify API, backup trigger paths, most thresholds, Telegram, etc.
- Do not claim Coolify/backup are per-server until a later slice.

## Do not

- Add more global env knobs that belong on a server row (Coolify URL/token, backup cmd per host).
- Half-migrate (UI without wiring `getSshClient(serverId)`).
- Mass-edit unrelated docs/markdown while touching this.
- Call `getSshClient()` without `serverId`.

## Later slices (only when user asks)

1. Coolify API URL/token per server (or per app).
2. Backup paths / trigger per server.
3. Deprecate global `SSH_*` once all rows have secrets.

## Default when unsure

Stop and ask. Prefer one vertical slice over a repo-wide rewrite.
